    "ADO-PERSIST",
    "ADO-DISCONNECT",
    "ADO-BATCH"
  ],
  "description": "ADO-PERSIST/ADO-DISCONNECT with ADTG: a client static batch-optimistic Recordset of SELECT ID, Code, V, V2, S FROM W ORDER BY ID (read/write copy) has S of row 1 changed, row 2 deleted and a row inserted (ID 40, Code \"w40\"), and is saved as ADTG (file kept) and closed; the file is reopened connectionless with adCmdFile (State, RecordCount, each row's Status, S, OriginalValue and UnderlyingValue); ActiveConnection is set by reference to the read/write Connection (State) and UpdateBatch(adAffectAll) is called (Errors); then the Recordset property \"Unique Table\" is set to \"W\" and UpdateBatch called again (Errors); the rows again and the stored rows through Execute. Asks whether pending changes survive the file and whether a reopened recordset can submit them.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
